A swift white flash across the net,
A game of speed and quick finesse.
The shuttlecock takes sudden flight,
A feathered dart of pure delight.

With steady grip and watchful eye,
We track the rocket through the sky.
A delicate drop, a sudden smash,
Decided in a lightning flash.

The sneakers squeak upon the floor,
As breathless players chase the score.
A blur of motion, fierce and grand,
The fastest racket in the land.
